# Æion Factory — credentials, one key per capability.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repository root and fill the values locally.
# `.env` is git-ignored; this template is committed and never contains a value.
#
# The rule this file exists for: the AI writes the code, so the AI must not hold the key that
# merges it. Every credential below carries exactly one role, and a process may only hold the
# roles it needs. `demo/factory/keys.py` enforces the roles; `demo/tests/test_factory_keys.py`
# proves it. Branch protection independently requires the configured exact-head CI checks.
# Fine-grained PAT scopes alone do not distinguish branch publication from merging; the
# supervisor's isolated roles enforce that distinction. Do not claim a stolen write PAT cannot merge.
#
# Create the GitHub keys as *fine-grained* personal access tokens, scoped to
# `OualidGuennif/aeion-autonomous-forum` only, with an expiry, and grant only the permissions in
# the comment above each name.

# Trusted source synchronizer only: clone/read. Model workers receive pinned public bytes, no key.
# GitHub permissions: contents:read, pull_requests:read (Contents = Read-only,
# Pull requests = Read-only).
GH_BUILD_KEY=

# The isolated publisher: one `aeion/build-*` branch and pull request against `main`.
# GitHub permissions: contents:write, pull_requests:write (Contents = Read and write,
# Pull requests = Read and write).
# The separately reviewed maintainer bootstrap also changes CI: it temporarily needs
# Workflows = Read and write on this repository only. Ordinary workers cannot change CI.
# Its process refuses merge operations and never holds release or inference credentials.
GH_API_KEY=

# The isolated release process: merges only after two independent model approvals, protected
# checks and exact-head required CI, then confirms the result on main.
# GitHub permissions: contents:write, pull_requests:write, administration:read (Administration
# = Read-only, to inspect main protection; no permission to change it).
# Never exported to an agent, a worker, the publisher or the review circuit.
GH_RELEASE_KEY=

# Inference: the supervisor relay and the two-vote review circuit. Never a GitHub key, and never
# in the same process as one.
OPENCODE_API_KEY=
